# Defense in depth for Cloudflare Workers static assets.
#
# `wrangler.jsonc` points assets at ./public, which never contains any of this.
# This file only matters if a deploy is ever misconfigured to use the repo root
# as the asset directory — which is exactly what Workers Builds auto-generated
# on 2026-10-27, uploading node_modules/workerd (137 MiB) and failing with
# "Asset too large" against the 25 MiB per-asset limit.
#
# Keep this list broad. It costs nothing when the asset dir is ./public.

**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.github
**/.wrangler
**/.DS_Store
**/*.sql
**/*.bak
**/*.env
**/.env*
**/src-tauri/target
src-tauri
supabase
node_modules
.git
cloudflare
scripts
package.json
package-lock.json
wrangler.jsonc
MASTER_PLAN.md
CODE_REVIEW.md
DEPLOYMENT.md
skills-lock.json
